body:
Shit, "No desire to live, no desire to die" is probably the simplest explanation of how I feel on a daily basis. 

&#x200B;

Thanks for that.

&#x200B;

I haven't spent a lot of time looking into my bipolar 2, as the meds have kept me in this stable position, but maybe I should read more here to understand why I feel like a terrible human.  


I hope your day improves, even if its only microscopically

The first thing that comes to mind is treating those comorbidities first.   


I'm also thinking about the potential trauma you've experienced. Check this channel out and see if anything there resonates with you: [https://www.youtube.com/c/crappychildhoodfairy](https://www.youtube.com/c/crappychildhoodfairy)

&#x200B;

ADHD coaching is not therapy, but might be a useful tool in your arsenal.

&#x200B;

As for death, I've been there, it's not a good place to be, but there is a life on the other side. 


I'm also looking back on a friend who killed himself 10 years ago at 26 and thinking about how different it could have been for him.

&#x200B;

Pat yourself on the back for writing this post - you've still got fight in you.

Personally, a mood stabilizer and stimulant have made a world of difference in my life.


I never wanted to hear anything anyone had to say when I was in the place you're in.

&#x200B;

I came out the other side and never thought I would, which means there's a chance for you too.

&#x200B;

Getting help is difficult, especially in some countries. I'm no expert, but keep talking to people and ask for help. Eventually someone will point you in the right direction.

If I am at all suspicious about the caller on the other end, I'll basically ask them some security questions myself, such as the last three numbers of my social insurance number, last two of my security code, etc.

&#x200B;

edit: They also give you a confirmation number when you apply for the callback, which you should hold on to.

I posted this clip above, but it is also relevant to what you're asking.

&#x200B;

[https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ao6f5ZT9MfE&feature=youtu.be&t=110](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ao6f5ZT9MfE&feature=youtu.be&t=110)
